      <title>A brighter side to sulfur dioxide</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00864-1</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Reviews Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 27 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00864-1"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43017-026-00864-1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;An article in Nature Geoscience finds that sulfur dioxide can form aerosols that act as seeds for cloud droplets, prolonging cloud brightening and increasing cloud reflectivity.</content:encoded>
